{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:0cm;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\nnormal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:\r\n12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed two storey rear extension,\r\nin conjunction with the gable end and large rear dormer roof extensions, would\r\nintroduce an incongruous, overly dominant and obtrusive form of development\r\nthat would fail to respect the form and proportions of the existing\r\ndwellinghouse, and the character and appearance of the neighbouring properties,\r\nto the detriment of the character and appearance of the existing dwellinghouse\r\nand the surrounding area, contrary to the high quality design aspirations of\r\nthe National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policy D3.D (1) and (11) of The\r\nLondon Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy\r\nDM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the\r\nadopted Supplementary Planning Document Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
